Type><SpatRepTypCd value="001" Sync="TRUE"/></spatRpType><searchKeys><keyword>Private School Universe Survey</keyword><keyword>PSS</keyword><keyword>Private Schools</keyword><keyword>National Center for Education Statistics</keyword><keyword>NCES</keyword><keyword>Private School Locations</keyword><keyword>U.S. Census Bureau</keyword><keyword>Education Demographic and Geographic Estimates Program</keyword><keyword>EDGE</keyword><keyword>Points</keyword><keyword>United States</keyword></searchKeys><idPurp>The Private School Universe Survey (PSS) consists of private school data submitted to the National Center for Education Statistics (NCES). The Census Bureau geocodes the PSS school locations for use in a geographic information system (GIS) or other geographic applications. NCES releases the point location data in the form of a shapefile and geodatabase for public use. </idPurp><idAbs>&lt;DIV STYLE="text-align:Left;"&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;The Private School Universe Survey (PSS) is conducted to generate biennial data on the total number of private schools, teachers, and students, and to build an accurate and complete list of private schools to serve as a sampling frame for NCES surveys of private schools. The PSS school location and associated geographic area assignments are derived from reported information about the physical location of private schools. The school geocode file includes supplemental geographic information for the universe of schools reported in the PSS school sample, and they can be integrated with the survey files through use of institutional indentifiers included in both sources.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;All information contained in this file is in the public domain. Data users are advised to review NCES program documentation and feature class metadata to understand the limitations and appropriate use of these data.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;</idAbs><idCredit>NCES EDGE

PSS products are not copyrighted. These products are free to use in a product or publication, however acknowledgement must be given to the National Center for Education Statistics as the source. The point information in the PSS school shapefile is for statistical research purposes only. Coordinates in the shapefile have six implied decimal places, but the positional accuracy of these coordinates may not be as great as the six decimal places suggest.</idCredit><resConst><Consts xmlns=""><useLimit>&lt;DIV STYLE="text-align:Left;"&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;DIV&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN&gt;https://www.usa.gov/publicdomain/label/1.0/&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;</useLimit></Consts></resConst><dataChar><CharSetCd value="004"/></dataChar><dataExt xmlns=""><geoEle xmlns=""><GeoBndBox><exTypeCode>1</exTypeCode><westBL>-159.713009</westBL><eastBL>-67.838572</eastBL><southBL>19.490814</southBL><northBL>64.874143</northBL></GeoBndBox></geoEle></dataExt><idPoC xmlns=""><rpIndName>Douglas Geverdt</rpIndName><rpOrgName>National Center for Education Statistics</rpOrgName><rpPosName>Administrative Data Division</rpPosName><role><RoleCd value="003"/></role><rpCntInfo xmlns=""><cntAddress addressType="postal"><delPoint>550 12th Street, SW #4176</delPoint><city>Washington</city><adminArea>DC</adminArea><postCode>20202</postCode><eMailAdd>Douglas.Geverdt@ed.gov</eMailAdd><country>US</country></cntAddress><cntPhone><voiceNum tddtty="">(202) 245-8230</voiceNum></cntPhone></rpCntInfo><displayName>Douglas Geverdt</displayName></idPoC></dataIdInfo><mdLang><languageCode value="eng" Sync="TRUE"/><countryCode value="USA" Sync="TRUE"/></mdLang><mdChar><CharSetCd value="004" Sync="TRUE"/></mdChar><distInfo xmlns=""><distFormat xmlns=""><formatName Sync="TRUE">Shapefile</formatName></distFormat><distTranOps xmlns=""><transSize Sync="TRUE">0.597</transSize></distTranOps></distInfo><mdHrLv><ScopeCd value="005" Sync="TRUE"/></mdHrLv><mdHrLvName Sync="TRUE">da